        "message": "LU-20076 tests: force a TXG instead of sleeping on ZFS\n\nOn ZFS, wait_delete_completed() and its helpers sleep 5 seconds\nfor each wait, twice when deletes were pending, whether or not\nanything was deleted. sanity-quota makes about 400 such sleeps per\nrun on ZFS, 18% of the run, and sanity about 100.\n\nThese estimated counts represent 2,000 seconds of fixed sleep in\nsanity-quota and 500 seconds in sanity, about 42 minutes combined\nper ZFS run, before the cost of force_sync. Rainshadow reports\n2,471 sanity-quota runs in review-dne-zfs-part-4 and 2,570 sanity\nruns in review-dne-zfs-part-1 over the last 30 days (October 30,\n2026). At those counts, these two groups alone spend about 1,730\nsuite-hours per 30 days in these sleeps. This estimates removed\nsleep time, not measured end-to-end savings; other suites are not\ncounted.\n\nThe wait only needs the freed space to come back. Forcing a sync\non the target does that at once, and it covers every target,\nwhere the sleep covered only the first MDT and the first OST.\n\nsetup_quota_test() also repeats the wait that the previous\ntest's cleanup_quota_test() has just done. Remove it.\n\nCallers that pass an explicit time keep their sleep: they wait\nfor more than the commit.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity fstype=zfs\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I4173dee00f7e5deb8fd385c4d85640221e2d126b\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70270\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
